    "page": 10,
    "text": "Theory, Prediction, and Experiment\n\n\n\n\n    • The Scientific Method depends on the statement of very clear theories about how the\n    world is like, usually in the form of differential equations.\n    • We then solve these differential equations, and the result is a prediction of what the\n    world is like when we actually measure it!\n    • Theory: The vocal folds are a membrane, so when it vibrates, the wave of vibration will\n    have equidistant peaks in the spectrum (which we call harmonics).\n    • The differential equations are many of the type we have already seen, but slightly\n    more complicated\n    • Prediction: if I measure any of your laryngeal vibration signals, they will have a\n    spectrum with equidistant harmonics.\n    • Let’s do an experiment to find out if this is true!!!!!",
